  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Explain why it is impossible to have a right-angled triangle with these properties.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Impossible: $\\dfrac{O}{A}>0$ because both side lengths are positive.",
          "worked": "$$\\tan\\theta=\\frac{O}{A}=-1$$\nThis would require one of $O$ and $A$ to be negative, but side lengths are positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Impossible: this requires $O=H$, but the hypotenuse is longer than either other side.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{O}{H}&=1\\\\O&=H\\end{align*}$$\nThis is impossible because the hypotenuse is longer than either other side.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Impossible: this requires $A=0$, but a triangle's side lengths are positive.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{A}{H}&=0\\\\A&=0\\end{align*}$$\nA triangle cannot have a side of length zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta>1$ or $\\cos\\theta>1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Impossible: this requires $O>H$ or $A>H$, but the hypotenuse is the longest side.",
          "worked": "For $\\sin\\theta>1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{O}{H}&>1\\\\O&>H\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\cos\\theta>1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{A}{H}&>1\\\\A&>H\\end{align*}$$\nBoth are impossible because the hypotenuse is the longest side.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
